# Vite+'s own hook runner. `vp staged` reads the `staged` block in the root
# vite.config.ts — that block is where the per-file checks live, not here.
#
# Only the flags that make the staged run deterministic belong in this file.

# --concurrent false: the tasks are ordered on purpose. `vp fmt` rewrites files
# in place, and lint and typecheck read them; run in parallel — which is the
# default — a formatter write can land under a reader mid-parse and fail a
# commit that has nothing wrong with it.
#
# --relative: hand tasks repo-root-relative paths. `git-hygiene.sh` matches
# paths like apps/server/src/*.ts, and the typecheck task maps a path to the
# workspace package that owns it; both want the path as the repo spells it.
vp staged --concurrent false --relative
